# turbo
.turbo

# local agent/harness state
#
# Sprint 09B.29 (C5) — everything here stays ignored EXCEPT `.claude/rules/*.md`.
#
# Those rule files are binding project constraints, not local state: they are
# what the agent actually loads, so a contributor or CI checkout without them
# is working to a different specification than the one this sprint was held to.
# Previously the whole directory was ignored and the rule survived only as a
# hand-copied duplicate under `docs/`, which had already begun to drift.
#
# The negation is deliberately narrow. A parent directory that is excluded
# cannot have its children re-included, so `.claude/` becomes `.claude/*` and
# each level is re-excluded in turn — `settings.local.json`,
# `scheduled_tasks.lock` and anything else added later stay ignored.
.claude/*
!.claude/rules/
.claude/rules/*
!.claude/rules/*.md

